1
00:00:02,115 --> 00:00:05,022
So at this point, we had a very close look

2
00:00:05,151 --> 00:00:08,381
at how we can configure the requests that

3
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:11,057
are sent and managed by HTMX.

4
00:00:12,665 --> 00:00:15,542
But it turns out that we can actually also

5
00:00:15,719 --> 00:00:19,031
configure the responses quite a bit and with

6
00:00:19,241 --> 00:00:19,369
them

7
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:23,794
also change the behavior of HTMX. And that's

8
00:00:23,826 --> 00:00:25,129
what I'll show you next.

9
00:00:26,847 --> 00:00:29,802
And I wanna start with submitting the form.

10
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:32,918
When we submit the form,

11
00:00:33,496 --> 00:00:36,725
we of course send this POST request to

12
00:00:36,885 --> 00:00:37,720
/login.

13
00:00:39,214 --> 00:00:39,439
Now,

14
00:00:40,001 --> 00:00:42,635
in that login route, we're then validating

15
00:00:42,828 --> 00:00:45,366
the inputs and you already saw what happens

16
00:00:45,542 --> 00:00:47,181
if an invalid input is entered.

17
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:51,469
But if we succeed, I'm currently not sending

18
00:00:51,501 --> 00:00:53,477
back anything. I'm sending back an empty

19
00:00:53,509 --> 00:00:54,039
response.

20
00:00:55,548 --> 00:00:57,190
Now, what we might wanna do

21
00:00:57,737 --> 00:01:00,086
if we're facing a login form like this

22
00:01:00,778 --> 00:01:03,336
is that when the user enters valid

23
00:01:03,368 --> 00:01:03,819
credentials

24
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,925
and we click login,

25
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:09,537
we might want to redirect the user to a new

26
00:01:09,683 --> 00:01:09,975
page.

27
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,726
So we might want to redirect to

28
00:01:16,087 --> 00:01:19,376
/authenticated here, for example, so to this

29
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:19,797
route.

30
00:01:20,854 --> 00:01:23,157
Now, of course, if you recall what you

31
00:01:23,157 --> 00:01:24,940
learned in earlier sections,

32
00:01:25,653 --> 00:01:28,167
we'll have a problem if we try to do that.

33
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:29,467
So here, if I

34
00:01:29,998 --> 00:01:32,606
reload and I enter a valid email

35
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,553
and then some valid password and I click

36
00:01:35,617 --> 00:01:36,004
login,

37
00:01:37,082 --> 00:01:39,495
you see the content of the next page is

38
00:01:39,778 --> 00:01:40,610
rendered here.

39
00:01:42,174 --> 00:01:44,918
It's rendered on the existing page. And that

40
00:01:44,934 --> 00:01:48,248
happens because, as you learned, HTMX by

41
00:01:48,457 --> 00:01:52,069
default follows redirects like this.

42
00:01:53,498 --> 00:01:55,697
And therefore, as a result, we

43
00:01:56,243 --> 00:01:58,908
don't load a new page in the browser, but

44
00:01:58,908 --> 00:02:03,259
instead HTMX gets the response of that new

45
00:02:03,773 --> 00:02:06,101
page or of this GET route here to be

46
00:02:06,101 --> 00:02:06,599
precise.

47
00:02:08,028 --> 00:02:10,821
And it then renders that into the target of

48
00:02:10,853 --> 00:02:13,993
the request we sent, so into this target

49
00:02:13,993 --> 00:02:14,236
here.

50
00:02:15,925 --> 00:02:18,540
Now, that sometimes is the behavior you

51
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:18,865
want,

52
00:02:19,417 --> 00:02:21,574
but sometimes you might want a real

53
00:02:22,009 --> 00:02:22,573
redirect.

54
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,696
And you can achieve that and change the

55
00:02:26,696 --> 00:02:30,336
behavior of HTMX by setting a specific

56
00:02:30,627 --> 00:02:32,459
header on the response.

57
00:02:33,922 --> 00:02:37,120
And here in Node, when using Express.js, you

58
00:02:37,152 --> 00:02:39,505
can do that by calling the setHeader header

59
00:02:39,505 --> 00:02:42,189
method on that response object before

60
00:02:42,189 --> 00:02:42,868
sending it.

61
00:02:44,502 --> 00:02:46,426
And the header I wanna set here

62
00:02:47,089 --> 00:02:50,698
is one of the special headers you can set on

63
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:53,269
the responses that are sent back and that

64
00:02:53,365 --> 00:02:55,293
will be handled by HTMX.

65
00:02:56,755 --> 00:02:59,890
Specifically, you can set the hx-redirect

66
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:01,354
response header to

67
00:03:01,885 --> 00:03:04,893
really trigger a client-side redirect to a

68
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:05,569
new page.

69
00:03:06,489 --> 00:03:10,853
So to not have HTMX take the response and

70
00:03:10,853 --> 00:03:13,352
render it into the target, but to really

71
00:03:13,627 --> 00:03:15,501
instead perform a redirect.

72
00:03:16,851 --> 00:03:19,148
And you see some other response headers and

73
00:03:19,181 --> 00:03:21,366
what they do here as well, but I'll get back

74
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:23,551
to some of them later. For the moment, let's

75
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:25,073
focus on that redirect header.

76
00:03:27,079 --> 00:03:30,079
So here it's HX-Redirect, which I wanna set,

77
00:03:30,954 --> 00:03:32,738
and I wanna set that to /authenticated.

78
00:03:35,686 --> 00:03:38,198
And this will then ensure that we indeed do

79
00:03:38,649 --> 00:03:41,628
redirect the user to that page and that that

80
00:03:41,628 --> 00:03:43,303
new page is therefore loaded

81
00:03:43,883 --> 00:03:46,896
and that HTMX will not just take the content

82
00:03:46,896 --> 00:03:49,000
of that page and render it somewhere else.

83
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:53,107
Now, one thing you'll need to do though is

84
00:03:53,203 --> 00:03:55,619
you should then not also send such a

85
00:03:55,635 --> 00:03:58,308
redirect response here, but instead just

86
00:03:58,308 --> 00:03:59,725
send an empty response.

87
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,579
But with that, if you save everything,

88
00:04:04,272 --> 00:04:05,223
if you reload here

89
00:04:05,788 --> 00:04:06,803
and you enter some

90
00:04:07,626 --> 00:04:09,528
valid credentials and you click login,

91
00:04:10,205 --> 00:04:12,132
you see now I'm really redirected to a new

92
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:15,047
page. We completely replaced the existing

93
00:04:15,079 --> 00:04:16,262
page with this one.

94
00:04:17,987 --> 00:04:19,985
And of course I can still go back and forth

95
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:21,998
now with the back and forward buttons.

96
00:04:22,659 --> 00:04:24,898
And that's the case because we now really

97
00:04:25,236 --> 00:04:26,461
redirected the user.
